      "message": "The cumulative limit check looks correct, but the commit message’s claim that nghttp2 tears down the connection appears inconsistent with the v1.69.0 or v 1.70.0 implementation. onDataChunkRecvCallback() returns NGHTTP2_ERR_TEMPORAL_CALLBACK_FAILURE (-521), whereas the DATA callback path [1] aborts only for errors below -900 [2]. Could you please clarify how the reported runtime test caused connection teardown?\n\n[1] https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2/blob/v1.69.0/lib/nghttp2_session.c#L6892\n[2] https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2/blob/v1.69.0/lib/nghttp2_session.c#L87",
